      'Soil is usually taken for granted. It is the brown material under our feet, the stuff of gardens and farms, apparently inert. In fact, a single handful of healthy soil contains more living organisms than there are people on Earth.',
      'This invisible world is extraordinarily productive. Bacteria and fungi break down dead leaves and roots, releasing nutrients that plants absorb. Earthworms burrow through the ground, creating channels that let air and water reach deeper layers. Without these small creatures, the soil would become compact and infertile.',
